Z||000000||goldfinger||10-12-2000||02:21 PM||||My system is as follows:<BR>HU: Pioneer Premier 920<BR>Speakers:<BR>Dash: Infinty Kappa 5 1/4 Comp set<BR>Doors: Infinty Perfect 6.1 comp set<BR>Sides: Infinty Kappa 4 x 6 plates<BR>Subs: 2 12" Infinty Perfect<BR>Amps:<BR>Subs: JBL 1200.1 <BR>Doors: JBL P180.2<BR>Sides & Dash: P80.4<P>This system should slam, it has all the necessarys like highs, mids, lows. It should play very high and sound crystal clear. I am going to put one 12" in the back of the car and one 12" perfect in the spare tire compartment with pips to get the bass inside the cab.I will take pictures of me making all this.<BR><P>------------------<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||1FST2M6||10-12-2000||03:11 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/in-n-out.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/in-n-out.jpg</A> <P>system in my old car<P>Xtant 1001dx w/lfq45<BR>driving 10" Kicker Solobaric 2ohm <P>Kenwood KAC-626<BR>driving 2 pairs of 4" MB Quart Co-axial<P>Sony CDX-C910<BR>(dead head)<P>would to hit 141db<P>installed by me, custom box by me and dad and LOTS OF HELP from Texas Instruments TI-82!<p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 10-12-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Seanh||10-12-2000||07:14 PM||||Umm. Why are you putting a sub in the back of the car? To play bass for the people on the sidewalk? Dont waste your money on putting a sub back there. I would either put 2 12's behind the seats. I did that, for SPL, I also put one 10 upfront and ported into the car. I also might recommed not putting speakers in the doors. Go for the kickpanels. I can get you boxes that hold them in the kickpanels, their $80 for the pair. I did this, and put 4" mids in the dash, 4" mids and 1" tweeters in the sail panels. 6.5 Polk Momos in the kickpanels. Polk momo 10" up front and 12"'s behind the seats. 5 2-channel Premier PRS amps in the trunk. Most of all, I must complement your choice for the various components, Premier Rules. I have the same headunit you do. Heres how my system is hooked up:<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Pioneer_2.gif">  <BR>It will blow the doors off just about anything that pulls up beside me wanting to show off stereos. Not to mention setting off car alarms left and right. <BR>Those are great calc's. I love my TI-92<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System<p>[This message has been edited by Seanh (edited 10-12-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Formula||10-12-2000||07:28 PM||||I thought that you had to have all of the subwoofers and amps behind the front door line to compete in anything under extreme, and if you were in an extreme class they would happily hand you your a$$.... A fiero is not going to hit over 150 or so decibals, and your running a lot of cone area.  Just my thoughts, Im not sure about rules in anything except for mecca.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Seanh||10-12-2000||08:55 PM||||I removed the ash trys and mounted switchs, 3 under each one to controle the turn on lead to each amp. I can run any amps I wish to at any time. The subs for SPL do not have to be behind the front door line. I have done numerous installs putting subs in the floorboards of the front seats, only for SPL competitions. I have not yet competed with my Fiero yet, but I should be pulling quite a bit of decibals running the two 12's with 1000Watts RMS and 2000Watts MAX. I am hoping it will push over 150D's. It just might. And if not, I can mess around with the setup until I get what I want. I am not usally competing in SPL's, but I will have to in the circuts I plan to do. <P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System||||reg||1
