Z||000008||1FST2M6||10-13-2000||09:23 PM||||it's REALLY hard to get decent SPL. i've got upgraded caps in my amp, 2 one farrad capacitors on the power leads, and i can melt a 200 amp fuse at will. Kicker thankfully warranties their stuff (i've replaced my solobaric quite a few times) it's 2 ohm unit and the Xtant is rated at 1000wrms@2ohms with the stock caps. the week shipment and upgrade (only $150) boosted it to 1123wrms@11.8v (43hz) at their bench test. in the .31cu.ft sealed enclouser the solobaric will jump past it's physical limits and selfdestruct! they are SUPER clear and fast but they WILL over extend. but like i said .. Kicker warrantys EVERYTHING!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">   got any pics Xtreme? if somone could find room to build a band pass enclouser the spl would be higher with the same amp and speaker.. but the space is a real PAIN to find. <P>------------------<BR>Shhh.. Top Secret! <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstcheeto_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||KRMFiero||10-13-2000||09:52 PM||||Where can you get Fiero Kick Panles for 80$???<P><BR>also 1FST2M6  whats with that turbo? I have a 84 2m4  know any way i can get a turbo in there?||||reg||1
Z||000010||Seanh||10-14-2000||12:19 PM||||I had a bad power issue at first with my system. I now have a 1400W Street Wires super batt. in the slightly deeper stock location. I used a Phionex (sp?) Gold 15 farad Distribution system. It is a cap and distribution block in one. It has two 1/0 guage inputs and eight 4 guage outputs. I also added a Street Wires 170 Amp Alt. My sub enclosure up front is a bandpass design. The behind the seats are sealed. I will not be competing until next summer. I am also thinking about building a custom enclosure to hold 2 10's up front and 4th order bandpass. About them kickpanels. I assume you mean the kickpanel enclosers I was talking about. I was told that he would have them on his page a few weeks ago, and there still not there. I emailed just now to ask whats going on. I will try to get some pictures for you guys.<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System||||reg||1
Z||000011||Black88GT||10-14-2000||12:43 PM||||Sean, you have been promising pictures since you got here.  I won't hold my breath this time either...<P>goldfinger, the 4x6 Kappas are too deep for the stock location.  Will need to modify..<P>Like someone else suggested, putting a sub in the trunk accomplishes nothing. If you are serious about competing, 2 12"s up front like Bryan Wilkinson did with his GT and port them into the cabin would work great.  This takes serious know how though and I am not sure what level of expertise you are at. I would put the amps anywhere but the trunk, it gets very hot in the trunk and amps and heat don't get along too well.  Personally, I don't like the amp behind the seat thing, unless you are in to massages while you drive.  I remember I rode in the back seat of a cavalier with 2 12s right up against the seat, when I got out of the car my back still felt like it was vibrating...<P>just some suggestions...<P><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD||||reg||1
